// CORPORATE KOMBAT — AFTER HOURS — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CORPORATE KOMBAT as late-night jazz-funk fusion — a game alternate of office, selectable from
// the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "a couple of remixes of this now... Surprise me!!"
// 
// AFTER HOURS: the office at 2 a.m. The cleaners are in, the boss is still upstairs, the lobby
// speaker is still playing the muzak to nobody — and then the night band: an 80s Japanese fusion
// record (Casiopea, T-Square, the Gran Turismo lounge) by way of Headhunters and Birdland.
// 
// THE HOOK is CORP FUNKHY 4's MELODY A (office.js lead25), note for note, as a T-Square unison:
// an EWI-style reed synth (bestPwmReedLead) with the FRPP-6 clean electric guitar; the EWI goes
// up the octave in the last head and the shout chorus. THE HARMONY is reharmonised, the tune never:
//   A  | Gm11 · C9 | Gm11 · C9sus4 | E♭maj9 · Cm11 | A♭maj9 · D13 |   (the Chameleon i–IV9)
//   B  | E♭maj9 | D9 | Cm9 · A♭maj9♯11 | D13 |
//   ii–Vs into the head and the shout: A♭maj9 · Am7♭5 · D7♭9
//   lobby (G major) | G6/9 · Am11 D13 | Em9 · Dm9 G13 | Cmaj9 · Am11 D13 | G6/9 · Am11 A♭13 |
//   (a ii–V into the IV, and the tritone sub A♭13 home — onto bar 1 and bar 5 alike)
// THE SOLO is the office's own Moog (Classic Mono, legato, 80 ms glide) three times round the B
// changes, decorated: | E♭maj9 | D7♭9 · Dm7♭5 G7alt | Cm9 · A♭maj9♯11 | Am7♭5 · D7alt |, the last
// D7alt turned into its tritone sub A♭13♯11 so the bass falls A–A♭–G into the breakdown.
// 
//   1–4    LOBBY, 2 A.M. — G major, once (the cabinet screen loops it): vibes on the lobby hook, Rhodes, fretless in two, cross-stick and shaker, through the lobby speaker
//   5–8    NIGHT SHIFT — the band comes in on the A changes: slap bass, clav through an auto-wah, Rhodes, kit with ghosts and hat barks, congas; a ii–V into
//   9–12   HEAD A — the hook as a T-Square unison: EWI + clean electric guitar, Rhodes comping
//   13–16  HEAD A — again, the clav and the congas in
//   17–20  HEAD B — the B melody in unison; the fretless takes over, the pad under it
//   21–24  HEAD A — the EWI up the octave over the guitar, slap back, into
//   25–28  SOLO 1 — the Moog over the B changes: the hook's cell restated over new chords
//   29–32  SOLO 2 — bebop eighths, enclosures, the dim arpeggio over G7alt; the ride
//   33–36  SOLO 3 — sixteenth runs to G6, the band at full tilt; A♭13♯11 (tritone sub) into
//   37–40  THE BOSS IS STILL UPSTAIRS — breakdown: kick, cross-stick, fretless, the vibes on the hook up the octave; a Simmons fill and a ii–V into
//   41–44  SHOUT CHORUS A — everyone in unison (EWI 8va, Moog, guitar, alto), the horn section in block chords, clav
//   45–48  SHOUT CHORUS B — the B melody, the same wall
//   49–52  SHOUT CHORUS A — the hook's last ending falls to A, and the loop goes back to bar 5
//   53–56  WIND-DOWN (after the loop) — the alto alone on the office's wind-down line, half time, Rhodes tremolo, fretless, pad
//   57–60  ENDING — the hook once more, quietly, EWI and guitar; G6/9, back in the lobby's key
// 
// Sounds: the EWI (bestPwmReedLead — the one PWM sound), FRPP-6 clean electric (frppCleanElectric),
// the Moog (Classic Mono · Solo, song-local), alto (mrdrSaxophone), vibes (mrdrVibraphone); Rhodes
// (rmndTineEP) through a stereo tremolo, clav (rm7AmClav) through an auto-wah, the horn section
// (mrdrHornStab) in block chords, an FM pad (rm7WarmPad); the bass a slap pair — FRPP-6 neck
// pickup thumb (frppBassNeck) and FM pops (mrdrSlapPop) — and the FRPP-6 fretless
// (frppFretlessBass) on the B, the solo, the breakdown and the lobby; the Breakbeat kit (ghost
// snare in its own lane) with the brighter Eighties hats (barks choked by the closed hat), Simmons
// toms, congas, a ride. No CRLS-1 voice anywhere.
// 
// Unlevelled lane by lane: lane gains set by reasoning against the remix targets (kick ≈ lead,
// bass 1–3 under, snare 3–6 under, pad 6–10 under, hats 12–16 under).
// Trailing master gain -4.5 dB.
// 60 bars at 104 (the office plays at 115), swing 56, 138 s; the loop 5–52 is 111 s.
// Written by work/local/_office-remix-after-hours.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs, which
// self-checks chord tones on the beats, chromatic notes as resolving approaches only, semitone
// clashes against the sounding chords, and the loop wrap; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
